# apps/mobile — copy to `apps/mobile/.env` (gitignored) and edit. #209.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the JS bundle at BUNDLE time, not read at runtime: after editing
# this value you must restart Metro (`npx expo start --clear`) — reinstalling the APK alone does
# nothing, because the old value is already baked into the bundle the APK loads.
#
# Pick ONE of the three routes below. Full walkthrough: docs/runbooks/mobile-android-build.md

# --- Route A: USB / `adb reverse` (default for a handset on a cable) -------------------------
# `adb reverse tcp:3000 tcp:3000` makes the handset's own localhost:3000 tunnel to the host's
# localhost:3000 over the USB cable. No Wi-Fi, no LAN IP, and NO Windows Firewall rule — the
# traffic never touches the network stack's inbound path. Must be re-run after every unplug,
# device reboot, or adb server restart.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1

# --- Route B: LAN IP (handset on the same Wi-Fi as the dev machine) --------------------------
# Needs (1) the host's current Wi-Fi IPv4, which is DHCP and changes; (2) an inbound Windows
# Firewall rule for TCP 3000 — the profiles here default inbound to Block, and without the rule
# this route fails as a connection timeout that looks exactly like a wrong URL.
# Find the IP:  ipconfig  →  "Wireless LAN adapter Wi-Fi" → IPv4 Address
# (10.231.90.81 on this machine as of 2026-08-04 — verify, do not trust)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://<HOST-WIFI-IPV4>:3000/api/v1

# --- Route C: Android emulator ---------------------------------------------------------------
# 10.2.2.2 is wrong; 10.0.2.2 is the emulator's alias for the host's loopback. This is also the
# hardcoded fallback in src/api/client.ts when no .env is present — which is why a physical
# handset with no .env silently routes nowhere.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3000/api/v1
